1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,440
Its empire once covered a
quarter of the world's land.

2
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:06,071
But it all began with
a ring of stones.

3
00:00:06,111 --> 00:00:09,991
Around 2500 BC, the giant
stones of Stonehenge

4
00:00:10,031 --> 00:00:12,219
rise on Salisbury Plain.

5
00:00:12,259 --> 00:00:14,459
In the year 122,
Roman soldiers

6
00:00:14,499 --> 00:00:17,848
build Hadrian's Wall,
from coast to coast.

7
00:00:17,888 --> 00:00:21,048
In 1066, William the
Conqueror wins at Hastings,

8
00:00:21,088 --> 00:00:23,687
and stone castles rise.

9
00:00:23,727 --> 00:00:26,407
In 1599, Shakespeare's
Globe theatre

10
00:00:26,447 --> 00:00:28,602
opens beside the Thames.

11
00:00:28,642 --> 00:00:31,002
In 1707, England
and Scotland

12
00:00:31,042 --> 00:00:33,246
unite as Great Britain.

13
00:00:33,286 --> 00:00:36,766
In 1830, the first railway
between two cities opens,

14
00:00:36,806 --> 00:00:39,389
from Liverpool
to Manchester.

15
00:00:39,429 --> 00:00:41,669
In 1940, bombs
fall on London

16
00:00:41,709 --> 00:00:44,737
night after night,
but the city carries on.

17
00:00:44,777 --> 00:00:47,477
Today, about 69 million
people call it home,

18
00:00:47,517 --> 00:00:51,385
in England, Scotland,
Wales and Northern Ireland.

19
00:00:51,425 --> 00:00:55,210
Which era would you
visit? Tell us below.

